From 9145045191a1f63315c61e66ae874c46272875ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shaun Adams <s.adams@f5.com>
Date: Tue, 16 Jun 2026 15:36:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] mt-log-telemetry-tenant: per-tenant log isolation +
 tenant_id Prometheus label
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Closes the cross-tenant data leak in /api/logs* and Prometheus
metrics. Field-reported symptom: every tenant in the UI saw every
other tenant's request history because:

  - logstore.Log had no `tenant_id` column.
  - logstore *gorm.DB had no GORM scope callback registered (patch2's
    callback was wired into configstore only).
  - logging plugin's PreLLMHook had the resolver-stamped ctx in hand
    but had nowhere to put the tenant id.
  - telemetry plugin's defaultBifrostLabels listed every governance
    dimension (team, customer, virtual_key, business_unit) EXCEPT
    tenant — so `bifrost_requests_total` aggregated across tenants.

Storage side
* framework/logstore/tables.go — `TenantID` field on Log with
  `default:default` schema default + indexed.
* framework/logstore/migrations.go — `migrationAddLogsTenantIDColumn`
  adds the column and backfills 'default' for existing rows.
  Idempotent (HasColumn guard); rollback drops the column.
* framework/logstore/tenant_scope.go (new) — mirror of configstore's
  scope callback. The two packages cycle on direct imports
  (configstore -> logstore for log writes; logstore ->
  configstore/tables for VK joins), so the ~80 lines of callback are
  duplicated here rather than shared via a third package — that
  refactor is a separate cleanup, this patch is the minimum-viable
  isolation fix.
* framework/logstore/sqlite.go + postgres.go — call
  RegisterTenantScopes on the runtime *gorm.DB immediately after open
  (after migrations have run on the throwaway / background-ctx pool
  so the scope predicate doesn't fire on migration paths).

Plugin side
* plugins/logging/operations.go — insertInitialLogEntry reads the
  tenant id off BifrostContext and stamps it on the Log struct
  before CreateIfNotExists. Belt-and-braces with the INSERT scope
  callback: explicit stamp at construction time is clearer for
  background paths (async-job completion) than relying on the gorm
  hook.
* plugins/logging/go.mod — add multitenant module dep.
* plugins/telemetry/main.go — add `tenant_id` to defaultBifrostLabels
  and populate labelValues from BifrostContext. Prometheus treats ""
  as a valid label value, so single-tenant deployments get an
  unlabelled "tenant_id=\"\"" bucket without any code changes.
* plugins/telemetry/go.mod — add multitenant module dep.

Read side
* No /api/logs handler changes needed. The handlers already go
  through RDBLogStore.ScopedDB(ctx), so the GORM scope callback fires
  automatically on every SearchLogs / GetLogStats / etc. query and
  appends `WHERE logs.tenant_id = '<header>'`.

Regression test
* framework/logstore/tenant_scope_test.go (new) —
  TestLogTenantIsolation writes a row as tenant A and asserts tenant
  B cannot read it via ScopedDB; the INSERT callback also auto-
  stamps tenant_id from ctx even when the caller leaves the struct
  field empty. TestLogTenantIsolation_NoCtxTenant covers the single-
  tenant fallback (no header → scope short-circuits → both rows
  visible) so we don't regress OSS behaviour.

Ref: https://jira.f5net.com/browse/XC-25496
